## Server-side locale (`src/i18n/server.ts`)

```ts
import { cookies, headers } from "next/headers";
import { DEFAULT_LOCALE, isLocale, type Locale } from "./index";

export { LOCALES, LOCALE_META, DEFAULT_LOCALE, isLocale, dirFor, makeT } from "./index";
export type { Locale } from "./index";

export const LOCALE_COOKIE = "hrb_locale";

export async function getLocale(): Promise<Locale> {
  try {
    const c = await cookies();
    const v = c.get(LOCALE_COOKIE)?.value;
    if (isLocale(v)) return v;
  } catch {}
  try {
    const h = await headers();
    const al = h.get("accept-language") ?? "";
    const parts = al.split(",").map((p) => {
      const [tag, ...attrs] = p.trim().split(";");
      const qAttr = attrs.find((a) => a.trim().startsWith("q="));
      const q = qAttr ? parseFloat(qAttr.split("=")[1]) : 1;
      return { tag: tag.toLowerCase().split("-")[0], q: isNaN(q) ? 1 : q };
    }).sort((a, b) => b.q - a.q);
    for (const p of parts) if (isLocale(p.tag)) return p.tag;
  } catch {}
  return DEFAULT_LOCALE;
}
```

**Pitfall #39 — `makeT` MUST be re-exported from `server.ts`:** any
server component that does `import { makeT } from "@/i18n/server"`
gets `TypeError: makeT is not a function` if `server.ts` doesn't
re-export it. Add the re-export line the moment you create
`server.ts` — don't wait for the first layout import to fail.

**Pitfall #40 — `LOCALE_COOKIE` constant:** define it ONCE in
`server.ts` and import from there. Defining it locally in
`middleware.ts` causes drift if the cookie name changes.

