## Root layout (`src/app/layout.tsx`)

```tsx
import { Cairo, Inter } from "next/font/google";
import { getLocale, dirFor } from "@/i18n/server";

const cairo = Cairo({ subsets: ["arabic"], variable: "--font-cairo", display: "swap" });
const inter = Inter({ subsets: ["latin"], variable: "--font-inter", display: "swap" });

export default async function RootLayout({ children }: { children: React.ReactNode }) {
  const locale = await getLocale();
  const dir = dirFor(locale);
  return (
    <html lang={locale} dir={dir} className={`${cairo.variable} ${inter.variable}`}>
      <body className={dir === "rtl" ? "font-['Cairo',sans-serif]" : "font-['Inter',sans-serif]"}>
        {children}
      </body>
    </html>
  );
}
```

**Pitfall #45 — font switch per locale:** set BOTH Cairo and Inter
as CSS variables, then pick `font-family` in `<body>` based on
`dir`. Cairo's Arabic glyphs are gorgeous; Inter's Latin is
neutral. Mixing Cairo for LTR languages wastes bandwidth on
Latin glyphs it doesn't have.

**Pitfall #46 — `<html lang>` and `<html dir>`:** Next 15 sets
these on first render. If you mutate `dir` from a client component
mid-session (e.g. user toggles language), you need to update
`document.documentElement.dir` from the LanguageSwitcher, OR
force a full reload via `window.location.reload()` instead of
`router.refresh()`.

