# Pitfall 11.3b: Patching only 2 of 3 dictionaries

When adding new i18n keys to all 3 locale files (en/ar/fr), it's easy to
accidentally skip one file — the patches succeed silently and `tsc --noEmit`
passes because dictionary keys are not type-checked.

**Symptom**: a different locale's text leaks into the unchecked locale.
Real example (2026-07-01, HR Bridge): `nav.admin` was added to EN and AR
but NOT to FR. The French sidebar showed the Arabic word "المشرف" instead
of "Admin" because the missing key fell through to the Arabic entry.

**Detection**: browser-verify ALL 3 locales after any dictionary update.
`tsc` and `build` will NOT catch this. A quick grep catches it pre-browser:

```bash
for KEY in nav.admin common.workspace webhooks.group.employee; do
  for DICT in en ar fr; do
    grep -q "\"$KEY\"" src/i18n/dictionaries/$DICT.ts || echo "MISSING: $KEY in $DICT"
  done
done
```

**Fix**: patch the missing dictionary file(s) and re-verify with browser
in that locale to confirm the foreign text is gone.

**Prevention**: when adding N new keys across 3 dictionaries, always do
a final `grep -c "$KEY" src/i18n/dictionaries/*.ts` for each key to
confirm exactly 3 matches (one per locale) before declaring done.

---

## Pitfall 11.3c: Patch tool inserts duplicate keys (TS1117)

When using `patch` to insert a batch of new common keys into a
dictionary, if any of those keys already exists (from an earlier sweep),
the result is a single TS object literal with two properties of the
same name. TypeScript flags it as `TS1117: An object literal cannot
have multiple properties with the same name` but the error position
is the SECOND occurrence — which can be 1000+ lines after the original,
making it look unrelated.

**Symptom** (HR Bridge, 2026-07-04):
```
src/i18n/dictionaries/en.ts(941,3): error TS1117
src/i18n/dictionaries/en.ts(942,3): error TS1117
```
Lines 941-942 looked like unrelated `perm.payroll.*` keys — actually the
duplicates were `common.required` and `common.optional` that already
existed at lines 57-58 and had been re-inserted by the patch.

**Detection** (always run after dictionary patches):
```bash
npx tsc --noEmit 2>&1 | grep TS1117
# if non-empty: for each dup key, keep ONE definition and delete the other
```

**Prevention**: before inserting a batch of new common keys, grep
the target dictionary for each candidate key first:
```bash
for K in common.required common.optional common.retry; do
  echo "=== $K ==="
  grep -n "\"$K\"" src/i18n/dictionaries/en.ts
done
```
If a key already exists, skip the insert and instead add any new
translations under the existing entry.

---

## StatusBadge + StatusFromKey — semantic status pills with i18n binding

When many list pages render `pending` / `approved` / `rejected` /
`connected` / `expiring` as raw text or all-grey pills, build one
`StatusBadge` component with a status-string-to-(variant, i18n-key)
mapper. This:

- Gives every page consistent visual status colors (success=emerald,
  warning=amber, danger=rose, info=sky, neutral=slate, purple=indigo).
- Forces every status string to be i18n-bound, preventing the
  "leaked foreign word" bug above.
- Lets new pages get correct status badges by just passing a string:
  `<StatusFromKey status={row.status} />`.

Skeleton (drop into `src/components/StatusBadge.tsx`):

```tsx
import { useT } from "@/i18n/useT";

type Variant = "success" | "warning" | "danger" | "info" | "neutral" | "purple";
const VARIANT_CLASSES: Record<Variant, string> = {
  success: "bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-700 ring-emerald-200 dark:bg-emerald-900/30 dark:text-emerald-300 dark:ring-emerald-800",
  warning: "bg-amber-100 text-amber-700 ring-amber-200 dark:bg-amber-900/30 dark:text-amber-300 dark:ring-amber-800",
  danger:  "bg-rose-100 text-rose-700 ring-rose-200 dark:bg-rose-900/30 dark:text-rose-300 dark:ring-rose-800",
  info:    "bg-sky-100 text-sky-700 ring-sky-200 dark:bg-sky-900/30 dark:text-sky-300 dark:ring-sky-800",
  neutral: "bg-slate-100 text-slate-700 ring-slate-200 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-300 dark:ring-slate-700",
  purple:  "bg-indigo-100 text-indigo-700 ring-indigo-200 dark:bg-indigo-900/30 dark:text-indigo-300 dark:ring-indigo-800",
};

export function StatusBadge({ variant = "neutral", children, className = "", size = "sm" }: {
  variant?: Variant; children: React.ReactNode; className?: string; size?: "sm" | "md";
}) {
  const sizeClass = size === "sm" ? "text-[10px] px-2 py-0.5" : "text-xs px-2.5 py-1";
  return (
    <span className={`inline-flex items-center gap-1 font-semibold rounded-full ring-1 ring-inset ${sizeClass} ${VARIANT_CLASSES[variant]} ${className}`}>
      {children}
    </span>
  );
}

const STATUS_MAP: Record<string, { variant: Variant; i18nKey: string }> = {
  // leave
  pending:   { variant: "warning", i18nKey: "leave.statusPending" },
  approved:  { variant: "success", i18nKey: "leave.statusApproved" },
  rejected:  { variant: "danger",  i18nKey: "leave.statusRejected" },
  cancelled: { variant: "neutral", i18nKey: "leave.statusCancelled" },
  // crm
  lead:      { variant: "info",    i18nKey: "crm.statusLead" },
  prospect:  { variant: "purple",  i18nKey: "crm.statusProspect" },
  active:    { variant: "success", i18nKey: "crm.statusActive" },
  // documents / integrations / webhooks / recruitment — add the rest
  valid:     { variant: "success", i18nKey: "documents.statusValid" },
  expiring:  { variant: "warning", i18nKey: "documents.statusExpiring" },
  expired:   { variant: "danger",  i18nKey: "documents.statusExpired" },
  connected:    { variant: "success", i18nKey: "integrations.statusConnected" },
  disconnected: { variant: "danger",  i18nKey: "integrations.statusDisconnected" },
};

export function StatusFromKey({ status, size }: { status: string; size?: "sm" | "md" }) {
  const { t } = useT();
  const entry = STATUS_MAP[status];
  if (!entry) return <StatusBadge variant="neutral" size={size}>{status}</StatusBadge>;
  return <StatusBadge variant={entry.variant} size={size}>{t(entry.i18nKey)}</StatusBadge>;
}
```

