## EmptyState — every list page needs one

When a list page (leave requests, customers, webhooks, automations,
audit log, documents, candidates) has zero records, the page shows a
blank section under the filter bar and looks broken. Build a single
`<EmptyState>` component and use it everywhere.

Skeleton (drop into `src/components/EmptyState.tsx`):

```tsx
"use client";
import { useT } from "@/i18n/useT";

export default function EmptyState({
  title, description, icon, action, variant = "default",
}: {
  title?: string; description?: string;
  icon?: string | React.ReactNode;
  action?: { label: string; onClick: () => void; href?: string };
  variant?: "default" | "compact";
}) {
  const { t } = useT();
  const paddingClass = variant === "compact" ? "py-8" : "py-16";
