# MENA creative features — Hijri dates, regional multi-currency pricing, agency billing rollups, agency onboarding wizard, ZATCA invoice printing, branded invite emails, DNS verification wizard

Reference for shipping the small-but-delightful Arabic/MENA touches that turn
a generic SaaS into something that feels built for the region. Captured
2026-06-26 from the Q.af Phase 8 + 8b work.

---

## 1. Hijri (Umm al-Qura) "today" widget — zero deps

The web platform Intl API ships with full Hijri support out of the box,
including the Umm al-Qura calendar (Saudi Arabia's official astronomical
calendar). No npm package, no API call, no timezone math.

**Server-safe locale strings:**

| Need                       | Locale string                               | Notes                                  |
| -------------------------- | ------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------- |
| Gregorian Arabic           | `ar-SA-u-nu-arab`                           | Arabic-Indic numerals (٠١٢٣…)          |
| Hijri (Umm al-Qura) Arabic | `ar-SA-u-ca-islamic-umalqura-nu-arab`       | `ca=` is the calendar extension        |
| Hijri Latin (for parts)    | `ar-SA-u-ca-islamic-umalqura-nu-latn`       | Latin numerals, parseable with Number  |

**The full client widget (`src/components/HijriToday.tsx`):**

```tsx
"use client";
import { useEffect, useState } from "react";

type Formatted = { gregorian: string; hijri: string; weekday: string };

function format(d: Date): Formatted {
  return {
    gregorian: new Intl.DateTimeFormat("ar-SA-u-nu-arab", {
      weekday: "long", day: "numeric", month: "long", year: "numeric",
    }).format(d),
    hijri: new Intl.DateTimeFormat("ar-SA-u-ca-islamic-umalqura-nu-arab", {
      day: "numeric", month: "long", year: "numeric",
    }).format(d),
    weekday: new Intl.DateTimeFormat("ar-SA-u-nu-arab", { weekday: "long" }).format(d),
  };
}

// Approximate Hijri holidays for the current solar day. Static list — production
// should consult an authoritative lunar API.
const HIJRI_HOLIDAYS: { day: number; month: number; name: string; emoji: string }[] = [
  { day: 1,  month: 1,  name: "رأس السنة الهجرية",   emoji: "🌙" },
  { day: 10, month: 1,  name: "يوم عاشوراء",         emoji: "✨" },
  { day: 12, month: 3,  name: "المولد النبوي",       emoji: "🕌" },
  { day: 27, month: 7,  name: "ليلة الإسراء والمعراج", emoji: "🌌" },
  { day: 1,  month: 9,  name: "أول أيام رمضان",     emoji: "🌅" },
  { day: 27, month: 9,  name: "ليلة القدر",          emoji: "⭐" },
  { day: 1,  month: 10, name: "عيد الفطر",           emoji: "🎉" },
  { day: 9,  month: 12, name: "يوم عرفة",            emoji: "🤲" },
  { day: 10, month: 12, name: "عيد الأضحى",          emoji: "🐑" },
];

function currentHijriParts(d: Date): { day: number; month: number; year: number } {
  try {
    const parts = new Intl.DateTimeFormat("ar-SA-u-ca-islamic-umalqura-nu-latn", {
      day: "numeric", month: "numeric", year: "numeric",
    }).formatToParts(d);
    const get = (t: string) => Number(parts.find((p) => p.type === t)?.value ?? "0");
    return { day: get("day"), month: get("month"), year: get("year") };
  } catch { return { day: 0, month: 0, year: 0 }; }
}

export default function HijriToday({ variant = "landing" }: { variant?: "landing" | "compact" }) {
  const [data, setData] = useState<Formatted | null>(null);
  const [holiday, setHoliday] = useState<{ name: string; emoji: string } | null>(null);

  useEffect(() => {
    const d = new Date();
    setData(format(d));
    const h = currentHijriParts(d);
    const match = HIJRI_HOLIDAYS.find((x) => x.day === h.day && x.month === h.month);
    if (match) setHoliday({ name: match.name, emoji: match.emoji });
  }, []);

  if (!data) return null;
  // ... return landing or compact JSX
}
```

**Embed it on the landing page via dynamic import (SSR drift safe):**

```tsx
// src/app/page.tsx
import dynamic from "next/dynamic";
const HijriToday = dynamic(() => import("@/components/HijriToday"), { ssr: false });

// inside the hero section, before </section>:
<div className="hijri-row container"><HijriToday /></div>
```

`ssr: false` is required because the Intl output can differ between server and
client locales (server might be `en-US`, browser is `ar-SA`). The `useEffect`
ensures the widget renders only after hydration so there's no mismatch warning.

**CSS (glass card under hero):**

```css
.hijri-today {
  display: inline-flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 4px;
  padding: 14px 20px; border-radius: 18px;
  background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(111,44,255,.08), rgba(0,194,255,.06), rgba(26,232,164,.06));
  border: 1px solid rgba(111,44,255,.18);
  backdrop-filter: blur(6px);
  text-align: start; min-width: 220px;
}
.hijri-today-hijri { font-size: 22px; font-weight: 800; color: #2b2540; line-height: 1.3; }
.hijri-today-holiday {
  margin-top: 4px; padding: 6px 10px;
  background: linear-gradient(90deg, #fff7e6, #fff0f0);
  border: 1px dashed #f59e0b; border-radius: 10px;
  font-size: 13px; color: #92400e; font-weight: 600;
}
```

