## 4. Tenant ownership transfer endpoint pattern

`POST /api/tenants/[id]/transfer` — move workspace ownership to another user
by email. Used during agency offboarding, customer M&A, founder handoff, and
accidental-personal-workspace conversion.

```ts
type Params = { params: Promise<{ id: string }> };

export async function POST(req: NextRequest, ctx: Params) {
  const { id: tenantId } = await ctx.params;
  const auth = await getAuth();
  if (!auth) return NextResponse.json({ error: "unauthorized" }, { status: 401 });

  const body = await req.json().catch(() => ({}));
  const toEmail = (body.toUserEmail ?? "").trim().toLowerCase();
  if (!toEmail) return NextResponse.json({ error: "missing toUserEmail" }, { status: 400 });

  // Require explicit confirmation — destructive operation.
  if (!body.confirm) {
    return NextResponse.json(
      { error: "confirmation_required", hint: "Send { confirm: true } to acknowledge ownership transfer." },
      { status: 400 }
    );
  }

  const tenant = await prisma.tenant.findUnique({ where: { id: tenantId } });
  if (!tenant) return NextResponse.json({ error: "tenant_not_found" }, { status: 404 });

  // Caller must be the current owner
  const mine = await prisma.membership.findUnique({
    where: { userId_tenantId: { userId: auth.user.id, tenantId } },
  });
  if (!mine || mine.role !== "owner") {
    return NextResponse.json({ error: "forbidden_owner_only" }, { status: 403 });
  }

  const target = await prisma.user.findUnique({ where: { email: toEmail } });
  if (!target) return NextResponse.json({ error: "target_user_not_found", email: toEmail }, { status: 400 });
  if (target.id === auth.user.id) {
    return NextResponse.json({ error: "cannot_transfer_to_self" }, { status: 400 });
  }

  const existing = await prisma.membership.findUnique({
    where: { userId_tenantId: { userId: target.id, tenantId } },
  });
  if (existing?.role === "owner") {
    return NextResponse.json({ error: "target_already_owner" }, { status: 409 });
  }

  // Demote every current owner to admin (keep continuity, don't lose all admins)
  await prisma.membership.updateMany({
    where: { tenantId, role: "owner" },
    data: { role: "admin" },
  });

  // Promote target (or create + promote)
  const newMembership = existing
    ? await prisma.membership.update({
        where: { userId_tenantId: { userId: target.id, tenantId } },
        data: { role: "owner" },
      })
    : await prisma.membership.create({
        data: { tenantId, userId: target.id, role: "owner" },
      });

  // Update target's active tenant on any active sessions
  await prisma.session.updateMany({
    where: { userId: target.id, expiresAt: { gt: new Date() } },
    data: { activeTenantId: tenantId },
  });

  // Audit log to stderr (no AuditLog table in schema)
  console.log(JSON.stringify({
    event: "tenant.transfer", tenantId,
    fromUserId: auth.user.id, toUserId: target.id,
    timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),
  }));

  return NextResponse.json({
    ok: true, tenantId,
    newOwner: { id: target.id, email: target.email, name: target.name },
    membership: newMembership,
  });
}
```

**Why each guard matters:**
- `confirm:true` — destructive operation; double-confirm in the UI as well.
- `forbidden_owner_only` — admins should not transfer ownership; only owners.
- `target_user_not_found` (400 not 404) — UX hint that the email is wrong, but
  don't 404 because the tenant DOES exist.
- `cannot_transfer_to_self` — no-op detection.
- `target_already_owner` (409) — conflict semantics, not a 400.
- `updateMany` demote-all-owners — prevents the "tenant has no admin" gap
  during the brief moment between demote and promote.
- `session.updateMany activeTenantId` — so the new owner lands on the right
  workspace when they next load the dashboard.

---

## 5. SidebarLayout import + NavKey extension pitfall

`src/components/SidebarLayout.tsx` uses NAMED exports — `export function
SidebarLayout` and (after the patch below) `export type NavKey = ...`. Common breakage:

```tsx
// WRONG — default import + non-exported type
import SidebarLayout, { type NavKey } from "@/components/SidebarLayout";
// → TS2613: Module has no default export
// → TS2459: 'NavKey' is declared locally but not exported
```

```tsx
// RIGHT — named imports + re-state the type locally
import { SidebarLayout } from "@/components/SidebarLayout";
type NavKey = "overview" | "links" | "domains" | "analytics" | "bio" | "settings"
            | "team" | "qr" | "ab" | "payments" | "api-keys" | "webhooks" | "agency";

// ... use active={"agency" as NavKey}
```

When adding a new dashboard section (e.g. "agency"), you have two options:

**Option A — re-state the NavKey locally** (one-off, no upstream change):

```tsx
import { SidebarLayout } from "@/components/SidebarLayout";
type NavKey = "overview" | "links" | "domains" | "analytics" | "bio" | "settings"
            | "team" | "qr" | "ab" | "payments" | "api-keys" | "webhooks" | "agency";
// ... use active={"agency" as NavKey}
```

**Option B — extend SidebarLayout** (proper, adds nav entry, exports NavKey):

Edit `src/components/SidebarLayout.tsx`:

```ts
export type NavKey = "overview" | "links" | "domains" | "analytics" | "bio"
                   | "settings" | "team" | "qr" | "ab" | "payments"
                   | "api-keys" | "webhooks" | "agency";

const NAV: Array<{ key: NavKey; href: string; label: string; icon: React.ReactNode; section?: string }> = [
  // ...existing...
  { key: "agency", href: "/dashboard/agency", label: "الوكالة", icon: <AgencyIcon />, section: "billing" },
];
```

Then any page can:

```tsx
import { SidebarLayout, type NavKey } from "@/components/SidebarLayout";
```

**Pitfall: inserting an icon function before another that already references it.**
If you add a new icon (e.g. `IconAgency`), insert it BEFORE the existing icons
in the file so it's defined when the NAV array references it. Look for the
function declaration — paste the new function definition above the existing
icon block, then add the nav entry. Don't try to use a forward-reference; TS
will complain `Cannot find name 'IconAgency'`.

Prefer option B for any new persistent nav entry — keeps the type single-sourced.

---

## 6. Agency self-service signup wizard (Phase 8b)

`/start-agency` + `POST /api/agencies/signup` — anyone with a Q.af account can
apply to become a white-label agency. The agency starts `active: false` and
awaits admin approval. The user's active tenant is auto-switched to the new
agency workspace on success.

**API (`POST /api/agencies/signup`):**

```ts
// src/app/api/agencies/signup/route.ts
import { NextRequest, NextResponse } from "next/server";
import { prisma } from "@/lib/prisma";
import { getAuth } from "@/lib/auth";

function slugify(s: string): string {
  return s.toLowerCase().trim()
    .replace(/[^a-z0-9\u0600-\u06FF-]+/g, "-")
    .replace(/^-+|-+$/g, "")
    .slice(0, 48);
}

export async function POST(req: NextRequest) {
  const auth = await getAuth();
  if (!auth) return NextResponse.json({ error: "unauthenticated" }, { status: 401 });

  const body = await req.json().catch(() => null);
  if (!body || !body.name) return NextResponse.json({ error: "name_required" }, { status: 400 });
  const name = String(body.name).trim().slice(0, 80);
  if (name.length < 2) return NextResponse.json({ error: "name_too_short" }, { status: 400 });

  const rawSlug = slugify(String(body.slug || body.name));
  if (!rawSlug) return NextResponse.json({ error: "invalid_slug" }, { status: 400 });

  let suffix = 0;
  let slug = rawSlug;
  while (await prisma.agency.findUnique({ where: { slug } })) {
    suffix++;
    slug = `${rawSlug}-${suffix}`;
    if (suffix > 50) return NextResponse.json({ error: "slug_unavailable" }, { status: 409 });
  }

  try {
    const agency = await prisma.agency.create({
      data: {
        slug,
        name,
        brandColor: body.brandColor ? String(body.brandColor) : "#7c3aed",
        billingEmail: body.billingEmail ? String(body.billingEmail).toLowerCase() : auth.user.email,
        active: false, // requires admin approval
      },
    });

    // Create the agency's first tenant + ownership membership.
    // NOTE: Tenant model has no `ownerId` field directly — ownership is via Membership.
    const tenant = await prisma.tenant.create({
      data: {
        name: `${name} — الرئيسية`,
        type: "agency_main",
        agencyId: agency.id,
      },
    });
    await prisma.membership.create({
      data: { userId: auth.user.id, tenantId: tenant.id, role: "OWNER" },
    });
    // Switch user's active tenant to the new agency workspace
    await prisma.session.updateMany({
      where: { userId: auth.user.id },
      data: { activeTenantId: tenant.id },
    });

    return NextResponse.json({
      agency, tenant: { id: tenant.id, name: tenant.name },
      message: "تم إنشاء الوكالة بانتظار موافقة المشرف.",
      pendingApproval: true,
    });
  } catch (e: any) {
    if (e?.code === "P2002") {
      return NextResponse.json({ error: "duplicate", field: e?.meta?.target?.[0] || null }, { status: 409 });
    }
    console.error("agency.signup", e);
    return NextResponse.json({ error: "internal_error" }, { status: 500 });
  }
}
```

**UI wizard (`/start-agency/page.tsx`) — 4-step flow:**

1. **Basic info** — name, auto-slug, brand color (preset swatches + custom picker)
2. **Billing contact** — email for ZATCA invoices (defaults to account email)
3. **Workspace name** — initial `agency_main` tenant display name
4. **Confirmation** — POST → show success card with the agency color as accent + CTA to dashboard

CSS pattern: progress dots at top (`agency-step-dot`/`.active`), centered card
(`agency-onboard-card`), brand color picker rows (`agency-color-swatch`).

Link from `/business` marketing page (the white-label tier) with a gradient CTA
block: "وكيل معتمد؟ انضم لشبكة وكالات Q.af".

**Pitfalls captured:**
- `Tenant` has no `ownerId` field — ownership is via `Membership.role === "OWNER"`.
  Trying `data: { ownerId: auth.user.id }` on `prisma.tenant.create` fails with
  `Object literal may only specify known properties, and 'ownerId' does not exist`.
- Switching the user's `activeTenantId` inside the signup endpoint is the
  friendly UX (they land on the agency workspace immediately) — but it makes
  them lose their previous "demo-tenant" active workspace. Use the dashboard's
  workspace switcher (`/dashboard/settings` or the sidebar's tenant selector)
  to move back.
- Approval flow: agencies start `active: false` so they don't get a public
  landing page, can't be linked from `/agencies`, and can't onboard customers
  until a super-admin flips `active: true` in `/admin/agencies`.

