## 7. Branded invite emails via `renderBrandedEmail`

`src/lib/agency.ts` ships a `renderBrandedEmail({brand, subject, bodyHtml, lang})`
helper that produces a transactional email with agency branding (logo, color,
footer). The tenant invite endpoint can use it instead of plain text.

**Pitfall caught during the Phase 8b wiring:** the original draft referenced
`link` and `inviterName` BEFORE they were declared. The fix — compute `link`
and `inviterName` FIRST, then pass them into the email template.

```ts
// inside /api/tenants/invite POST handler
import { renderBrandedEmail } from "@/lib/agency";

// 1. Compute the invite URL FIRST
const baseUrl = process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_HOSTS?.split(",")[0]
  ? `https://${process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_HOSTS.split(",")[0]}`
  : "https://q.af";
const link = `${baseUrl}/invite/${token}`;

// 2. Look up inviter name (optional)
const inviter = await prisma.user.findUnique({
  where: { id: auth.user.id }, select: { name: true, email: true },
});
const inviterName = inviter?.name || inviter?.email || "صديقك";

// 3. Render the branded email
const brand = tenant.agency ? {
  name: tenant.agency.name,
  brandColor: tenant.agency.brandColor,
  logoUrl: tenant.agency.logoUrl,
  emailFooter: tenant.agency.emailFooter,
} : {
  name: "Q.af",
  brandColor: "#7c3aed",
  logoUrl: null,
  emailFooter: null,
};

const subject = `دعوة للانضمام إلى ${tenant.name} على Q.af`;
const bodyHtml = `
  <p>${inviterName} يدعوك للانضمام إلى مساحة عمل <strong>${tenant.name}</strong> على Q.af.</p>
  <p style="margin:24px 0">
    <a href="${link}" style="background:${brand.brandColor};color:white;padding:12px 24px;
       border-radius:8px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:700;display:inline-block">
      قبول الدعوة
    </a>
  </p>
  <p style="color:#6b6786;font-size:13px">أو انسخ هذا الرابط: <br/><code>${link}</code></p>
  <p style="color:#6b6786;font-size:12px">صالح لمدة 7 أيام.</p>
`;

const email = renderBrandedEmail({ brand, subject, bodyHtml, lang: "ar" });
// Then send via your SMTP/Resend/SES layer using email.subject + email.html
```

**Always declare variables in dependency order** — `link` and `inviterName`
must be computed BEFORE `renderBrandedEmail` is called. If you use a structured
helper, declare-then-use; don't try to reference a variable inside a function
that is defined later in the same scope.

