## 9. ZATCA Phase-2 invoice — print-ready HTML + XML download

Two endpoints + one print-friendly page:

- `GET /api/invoices/[id]/xml` (tenant-facing) — generates UBL 2.1 XML with seller name (from agency if present), VAT math (15%), SHA-256 stamp.
- `/dashboard/invoices/[id]` — print-friendly HTML with bilingual labels (Arabic primary, English secondary), Hijri date alongside Gregorian, status pill, and `@media print` CSS that hides the toolbar.

**Schema pitfall — Payment has no `tenant` relation in Prisma:**

```prisma
model Payment {
  id        String  @id @default(cuid())
  tenantId  String
  // no `tenant Tenant @relation(...)` declared
}
```

So `prisma.payment.findUnique({ include: { tenant: ... } })` fails with
`Object literal may only specify known properties`. Fix: fetch separately:

```ts
const p = await prisma.payment.findUnique({ where: { id } });
if (!p || !p.invoiceNo) return notFound();
if (p.tenantId !== auth.tenantId) redirect("/dashboard/payments");
const tenant = await prisma.tenant.findUnique({
  where: { id: p.tenantId },
  include: { agency: true },
});
```

**Don't try to `(p as any).tenant = ...` runtime-assign** — TS narrows the
type and rejects. Use a separate `tenant` variable.

**Print CSS pattern:**

```css
@media print {
  .no-print { display: none !important; }
  .invoice-page { padding: 0; }
  .invoice-sheet { border: none; box-shadow: none; padding: 24px; }
  body { background: white !important; }
}
```

**VAT math:**

```ts
const total = p.amount; // halalas
const vat = Math.round((total * 0.15) / 1.15);
const subtotal = total - vat;
```

The 15% is statutory Saudi VAT (ZATCA). Production should read from a per-tenant
tax-rate field; EAU is 5%, Bahrain 10%, etc.

