# Phase 11 — PWA + Offline Mode + Push Notifications

Production-grade Progressive Web App layer for an Arabic-first multi-tenant
SaaS. Covers install prompts (Android + iOS), service-worker cache
strategies, an in-app notification center with unread badge + dropdown,
Web Push (VAPID), and an admin panel for managing subscriptions.

## Goal
- Install the app on phone/desktop (standalone window, home screen icon).
- Survive offline / flaky network via SW cache + dedicated `/offline` page.
- Push real OS-level notifications (Web Push API + VAPID) for tenant events.
- Show in-app notification bell with unread badge + dropdown history.

## File map (HR Bridge SA reference build, 2026-06-28)

| Path | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `public/manifest.json` | PWA manifest (name, icons, theme_color, display=standalone, start_url, scope) |
| `public/sw.js` | Service worker v2: precache core routes, network-first for API, cache-first for static, `/offline` fallback |
| `public/icon-192.svg` + `icon-512.svg` | PWA icons (any-format icons work; SVG preferred for size) |
| `src/app/offline/page.tsx` | Offline fallback page — **MUST be `"use client"`** if it has any onClick (see Pitfall #28) |
| `src/components/PWAInit.tsx` | Client component that registers the SW on mount (`navigator.serviceWorker.register('/sw.js')`) |
| `src/components/OfflineBadge.tsx` | Small floating "📴 غير متصل" badge that shows when `navigator.onLine === false` |
| `src/components/PushPermissionPrompt.tsx` | Asks for `Notification.requestPermission()` after first dashboard visit (skip if already granted/denied) |
| `src/components/InstallPrompt.tsx` | **Phase 11 NEW** — captures `beforeinstallprompt`, shows custom install card, iOS fallback instructions, 7-day dismissal cooldown via localStorage |
| `src/components/NotificationCenter.tsx` | **Phase 11 NEW** — bell icon + unread badge + dropdown, polls `/api/push/notifications` every 30s, outside-click close, mark-read on click, link to settings |
| `src/lib/push.ts` | **Phase 11 NEW** — VAPID-aware `sendPush({tenantId, userId?, type, title, body, url?})`. Persists a Notification row + fans out to active subscriptions, auto-disables 410 endpoints |
| `src/app/api/push/subscribe/route.ts` | GET (returns `vapidKey`), POST (save subscription), DELETE (disable) |
| `src/app/api/push/notifications/route.ts` | GET list (with `unread` count), PATCH mark-read (single id or `markAll: true`) |
| `src/app/api/push/send/route.ts` | POST — admin-only test endpoint that calls `sendPush()` |
| `src/app/dashboard/settings/notifications/page.tsx` | **Phase 11 NEW** — admin/manager UI: 3 status cards (Push permission, Install state, Stats), test push form, subscriptions table, recent notifications feed |
| `src/types/web-push.d.ts` | **Phase 11 NEW** — ambient declaration for `web-push` (no `@types` package) — see Pitfall #30 |

## Schema (Prisma) — required models

```prisma
model PushSubscription {
  id        String   @id @default(cuid())
  tenantId  String
  userId    String
  endpoint  String   @unique
  p256dh    String
  auth      String
  userAgent String?
  enabled   Boolean  @default(true)
  createdAt DateTime @default(now())
  updatedAt DateTime @updatedAt
  @@index([tenantId, userId])
  @@index([tenantId, enabled])
}

model Notification {
  id        String   @id @default(cuid())
  tenantId  String
  userId    String?  // null = broadcast
  type      String   @default("info") // info|success|warning|error|leave|payroll|sync|system
  title     String
  body      String
  url       String?  // deep link target
  read      Boolean  @default(false)
  createdAt DateTime @default(now())
  @@index([tenantId, userId, read, createdAt])
}
```

## VAPID key setup (first time only)

```bash
# generate a fresh pair
npx web-push generate-vapid-keys
# → Public Key: BPdMq...    Private Key: qP9sZ...

# .env
VAPID_SUBJECT="mailto:[email protected]"
VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY="BPdMq..."
VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY="qP9sZ..."
NEXT_PUBLIC_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY="BPdMq..."   # for client subscribe
```

`sendPush()` gracefully no-ops if env vars are missing — it still persists
the in-app `Notification` row so users see it in the bell dropdown.

## Service Worker contract

`public/sw.js` MUST:
- Set `const VERSION = "hrb-vN"` and cache core routes under `CACHE = VERSION + "-core"`.
- On `install`: skip waiting + `cache.addAll(CORE)`.
- On `activate`: delete old caches, `clients.claim()`.
- On `fetch`:
  - API + POST/PUT/DELETE → network-first, no cache
  - Static (/_next/static, /icon-*, /manifest.json) → cache-first
  - Navigation → network with `/offline` fallback when fetch fails

## Install prompt UX (Pitfall #28 + #29 + #32 + #33)

- `beforeinstallprompt` is fired **once** and only on Android/Chrome-class browsers. iOS Safari never fires it — always include the iOS fallback ("Share → Add to Home Screen").
- Stash dismissal in `localStorage` for 7 days to avoid nagging.
- Listen for `appinstalled` to hide the prompt.
- Default state: standalone window already installed → don't show.
- **#32 (PROMPT STACKING)**: Running `InstallPrompt` (z-40) + `PushPermissionPrompt` (z-50) as siblings on every page load causes two stacked bottom-right modals with different 3s/4s timeouts. Users see one modal, dismiss it, and immediately get the second. **Merge them into a single `PWABanner` component** that picks ONE prompt to show at a time (install > push, since install is only available in Chrome-class browsers) with `role="dialog"`, `aria-label`, and a session-level dismissal so re-navigating between pages doesn't re-show. See the PWABanner template below.
- **#33 (z-index trap)**: A `z-50` sibling stacked on top of `z-40` looks like a regression. Use the same z-index and let the merge component decide which prompt to render. Never stack two bottom-anchored modals.

## NotificationCenter UX checklist
- [x] Bell icon with absolute-positioned unread badge (red circle, ring)
- [x] Dropdown 360px wide, max-h 400px scroll
- [x] Polls every 30s + on `focus` event
- [x] Outside-click closes
- [x] Click on item → PATCH mark-read + navigate to `url`
- [x] Footer link to `/dashboard/settings/notifications` for full management
- [x] "تعليم الكل كمقروء" button only when unread > 0
- [x] Empty state with 📭 icon

## Verification ladder (Phase 11 additions)

After every PWA code change, in addition to the standard §verification:

```bash
# Build clean
npm run build                              # expect 0 errors, /offline prerendered

# PWA assets reachable
for p in manifest.json sw.js icon-192.svg icon-512.svg offline; do
  c=$(curl -s -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}" http://localhost:4000/$p)
  echo "$p → $c"                           # all 200
done

# Manifest sanity
curl -s http://localhost:4000/manifest.json | python3 -c "import sys,json; m=json.load(sys.stdin); print(m['name'], m['start_url'], m['display'], m['theme_color'])"

# Push API surface (cookie-authed)
for p in api/push/subscribe api/push/notifications api/push/send; do
  c=$(curl -s -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}" -b /tmp/c.txt http://localhost:4000/$p)
  echo "$p → $c"                           # 200 / 405 / 404 acceptable per method
done
```

Manual smoke (Chrome DevTools):
1. Open `/dashboard` → bell icon visible, unread = 0
2. DevTools → Application → Service Workers → confirm `sw.js` status = activated
3. DevTools → Application → Manifest → no errors, installability = ✅
4. Click 🔔 → empty state shows
5. Trigger a server-side `sendPush()` via `POST /api/push/send` (or call `sendPush()` from an action) → reload → bell badge shows 1, click → row appears, click row → marked read + navigates
6. DevTools → Network → Offline → navigate to `/dashboard/employees` → SW returns cached version or `/offline` fallback

## Pitfalls (Phase 11 — see SKILL.md for the canonical list)

- **#28** Pages with `onClick` MUST be `"use client"` — server components throw `Error: Event handlers cannot be passed to Client Component props` during prerender. Affects `/offline` page.
- **#29** `PushSubscription` has NO `user` relation in the Prisma schema — fetch users separately and join via `Map` by `userId`.
- **#30** `web-push` has no `@types/web-push` package — declare an ambient module in `src/types/web-push.d.ts` (template below) so `tsc --noEmit` and `next build` pass.
- **#31** `export const dynamic = "force-static"` + `onClick` = prerender error → either `force-dynamic` (loses static caching) OR convert to client component (preferred — keeps the page interactive AND static-cacheable as a client bundle chunk).

### Ambient module template (`src/types/web-push.d.ts`)
```ts
declare module "web-push" {
  export function setVapidDetails(subject: string, publicKey: string, privateKey: string): void;
  export function sendNotification(
    subscription: { endpoint: string; keys: { p256dh: string; auth: string } },
    payload: string,
    options?: any
  ): Promise<any>;
  export function generateVAPIDKeys(): { publicKey: string; privateKey: string };
  const _default: {
    setVapidDetails: typeof setVapidDetails;
    sendNotification: typeof sendNotification;
    generateVAPIDKeys: typeof generateVAPIDKeys;
  };
  export default _default;
}
```

### `sendPush` template (Phase 11 final)
```ts
// src/lib/push.ts — persists Notification + fans out web-push deliveries
import { prisma } from "./db";
import webpush from "web-push";

const VAPID_PUBLIC = process.env.VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY || "";
const VAPID_PRIVATE = process.env.VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY || "";
const VAPID_SUBJECT = process.env.VAPID_SUBJECT || "[email protected]";

let configured = false;
function ensureConfig() {
  if (configured || !VAPID_PUBLIC || !VAPID_PRIVATE) return;
  try {
    webpush.setVapidDetails(VAPID_SUBJECT, VAPID_PUBLIC, VAPID_PRIVATE);
    configured = true;
  } catch (e) { console.error("[push] VAPID config failed", e); }
}

export type PushInput = {
  tenantId: string;
  userId?: string | null;          // null = broadcast
  type?: "info" | "success" | "warning" | "error" | "leave" | "payroll" | "sync" | "system";
  title: string;
  body: string;
  url?: string;
  icon?: string;
};

export async function sendPush(input: PushInput) {
  // 1. Always persist the in-app notification first (so it appears in the bell
  //    dropdown even if Web Push isn't configured yet)
  const notif = await prisma.notification.create({
    data: {
      tenantId: input.tenantId,
      userId: input.userId ?? null,
      type: input.type || "info",
      title: input.title,
      body: input.body,
      url: input.url || "/dashboard",
    },
  });

  // 2. Bail early if VAPID isn't set up
  if (!VAPID_PUBLIC || !VAPID_PRIVATE) {
    return { sent: 0, total: 0, notificationId: notif.id };
  }

  ensureConfig();

  // 3. Fan out to subscribed devices
  const where: any = { tenantId: input.tenantId, enabled: true };
  if (input.userId) where.userId = input.userId;
  const subs = await prisma.pushSubscription.findMany({ where });

  const payload = JSON.stringify({
    title: input.title, body: input.body,
    url: input.url || "/dashboard",
    icon: input.icon || "/icon-192.svg",
    tag: notif.id,
  });

  const results = await Promise.allSettled(
    subs.map(async (s) => {
      try {
        await webpush.sendNotification(
          { endpoint: s.endpoint, keys: { p256dh: s.p256dh, auth: s.auth } },
          payload
        );
        return true;
      } catch (err: any) {
        // Auto-disable expired endpoints (Chrome 410, Firefox 404)
        if (err?.statusCode === 404 || err?.statusCode === 410) {
          await prisma.pushSubscription.update({ where: { id: s.id }, data: { enabled: false } });
        }
        return false;
      }
    })
  );
  return {
    sent: results.filter((r) => r.status === "fulfilled").length,
    total: subs.length,
    notificationId: notif.id,
  };
}
```

## When to use

- The product is mobile-heavy (field staff, on-the-go approvals) → PWA + push is mandatory.
- The product targets Saudi Arabia / MENA where 4G/5G is great but offline tolerance is still required (e.g. payroll runs in remote offices).
- Multi-tenant per-user notifications needed (broadcast + per-user).

## Trigger phrases
- "PWA", "installable app", "offline mode", "service worker", "web push", "notifications"
- "install on home screen", "add to home screen", "iOS PWA"
- "play store equivalent", "PWA install prompt", "push notifications"

## PWABanner — single-banner install + push prompt

When the codebase has both an `InstallPrompt` and a `PushPermissionPrompt` mounted globally, they will visually stack and confuse users. Merge them into ONE component that shows whichever is most relevant. Key design rules:

1. **One banner at a time**. Show install first (it's only available in Chrome-class browsers anyway). Fall through to push on subsequent mounts.
2. **Two-layer dismissal**: a 7-day `localStorage` TTL (hard nuke) and a session-only `sessionStorage` flag (don't re-prompt when the user re-navigates between dashboard pages).
3. **`role="dialog"` + `aria-label`** on the wrapper so screen readers announce it once, not twice.
4. **Same z-index for both flows** (z-40). Different z-indexes = users see "phantom" double-prompt when one hides.
5. **Anchor `bottom-*` with `md:right-6 md:max-w-sm`** so it docks to the right on desktop but spans bottom on mobile.
6. **Inline `urlBase64ToUint8Array` helper** scoped inside the component (only used here).
7. **On dismiss, persist the timestamp** with a single helper so you can see in localStorage exactly when the user last said no.

```tsx
"use client";
import { useEffect, useRef, useState } from "react";
import { useT } from "@/i18n/useT";

type BeforeInstallPromptEvent = Event & {
  prompt: () => Promise<void>;
  userChoice: Promise<{ outcome: "accepted" | "dismissed" }>;
};

type PwaKind = "install" | "push" | null;

const DISMISS_TTL_MS = 7 * 24 * 60 * 60 * 1000;
const SESSION_DISMISS_KEY = "hrb-pwa-dismissed-session";

function isDismissedRecently(key: string): boolean {
  if (typeof window === "undefined") return true;
  const raw = localStorage.getItem(key);
  if (!raw) return false;
  const ts = Number(raw);
  return Number.isFinite(ts) && Date.now() - ts < DISMISS_TTL_MS;
}

function persistDismiss(key: string) {
  try { localStorage.setItem(key, String(Date.now())); } catch {}
}

export default function PWABanner() {
  const { t } = useT();
  const [deferred, setDeferred] = useState<BeforeInstallPromptEvent | null>(null);
  const [installed, setInstalled] = useState(false);
  const [busy, setBusy] = useState(false);
  const [visible, setVisible] = useState<PwaKind>(null);
  const sessionDismissedRef = useRef(false);

  useEffect(() => {
    if (typeof window === "undefined") return;
    if (sessionStorage.getItem(SESSION_DISMISS_KEY) === "1") {
      sessionDismissedRef.current = true;
    }
    if (window.matchMedia("(display-mode: standalone)").matches) {
      setInstalled(true); return;
    }
    const navAny = navigator as Navigator & { standalone?: boolean };
    if (navAny.standalone === true) { setInstalled(true); return; }
    if (isDismissedRecently("hrb-install-dismissed")) return;

    const onPrompt = (e: Event) => {
      e.preventDefault();
      if (isDismissedRecently("hrb-install-dismissed")) return;
      setDeferred(e as BeforeInstallPromptEvent);
    };
    const onInstalled = () => { setInstalled(true); setVisible(null); };
    window.addEventListener("beforeinstallprompt", onPrompt);
    window.addEventListener("appinstalled", onInstalled);
    return () => {
      window.removeEventListener("beforeinstallprompt", onPrompt);
      window.removeEventListener("appinstalled", onInstalled);
    };
  }, []);

  useEffect(() => {
    if (installed || sessionDismissedRef.current || visible) return;
    if (deferred) { setVisible("install"); return; }
    if (typeof window !== "undefined"
        && "Notification" in window
        && Notification.permission === "default"
        && !isDismissedRecently("hrb-push-dismissed")
        && location.pathname.startsWith("/dashboard")) {
      setVisible("push");
    }
  }, [deferred, installed, visible]);

  function dismiss() {
    if (visible === "install") persistDismiss("hrb-install-dismissed");
    if (visible === "push") persistDismiss("hrb-push-dismissed");
    sessionStorage.setItem(SESSION_DISMISS_KEY, "1");
    sessionDismissedRef.current = true;
    setVisible(null);
  }

  if (installed || !visible) return null;
  const isInstall = visible === "install";
  const title = isInstall ? t("install.title") : t("push.title");
  const desc = isInstall ? t("install.desc") : t("push.desc");
  const action = isInstall
    ? (busy ? t("install.installing") : t("install.installNow"))
    : (busy ? t("push.enabling") : t("push.enable"));
  const borderClass = isInstall ? "border-emerald-200" : "border-indigo-200";

  return (
    <div
      className="fixed bottom-4 left-4 right-4 md:left-auto md:right-6 md:max-w-sm z-40 animate-fade-up"
      role="dialog"
      aria-live="polite"
      aria-label={title}
    >
      <div className={`bg-white/85 rounded-2xl p-4 shadow-2xl border ${borderClass} backdrop-blur-md`}>
        <div className="flex items-start gap-3">
          <div className="flex-1 min-w-0">
            <div className="font-bold text-slate-900 text-sm">{title}</div>
            <p className="text-xs text-slate-600 mt-1 leading-relaxed">{desc}</p>
            <div className="flex items-center gap-2 mt-3">
              <button onClick={isInstall ? /* install handler */ () => {} : /* subscribe handler */ () => {}} disabled={busy} className="btn-primary text-xs py-1.5 px-3">
                {action}
              </button>
              <button onClick={dismiss} className="btn-ghost text-xs py-1.5 px-3">
                {t("install.later")}
              </button>
            </div>
          </div>
          <button onClick={dismiss} aria-label={t("install.later")} className="text-slate-400 hover:text-slate-600 shrink-0 text-lg leading-none">×</button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  );
}
```
